"nodeIds":["cnm_058","cnm_p124","cnm_068","cnm_069","cnm_056","cnm_p101","cnm_066","cnm_067"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 210","reason":"Drawing through C a line parallel to AD produces a triangle with sides 5,12,13. Since 5²+12²=13², its area is 30 and its height to the 13-unit side is 60/13. The trapezoid area is ((52+39)/2)(60/13)=210.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_10A_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_067","cnm_112"],"id":"solution:auxiliary-right-triangle:b746884d00fe","label":"Create a 5-12-13 triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"auxiliary-right-triangle":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_177","cnm_p148","cnm_p149"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_177","cnm_p148","cnm_p149","cnm_055","cnm_067","cnm_112"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":8,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 4.0","reason":"The perpendicular projections of A and B leave equal overhangs of (10-4)/2=3. Thus B's foot is 7 units from D. Since B is the midpoint of DE, its horizontal coordinate is half that of E, giving DF=14 and CF=14-10=4.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1989_AMC_12_Q04","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p077","cnm_p105","cnm_064","cnm_067","cnm_110"],"id":"perpendicular-feet-and-midpoint","label":"Use perpendicular feet and the midpoint condition","methodDirectNodeIds":{"perpendicular-feet-and-midpoint":["cnm_055","cnm_125","cnm_121","cnm_185"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_125","cnm_121","cnm_185","cnm_p077","cnm_p105","cnm_064","cnm_067","cnm_110"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":8,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. 2 - 2√2","reason":"The only possible parallel pair requires cos x+tan x=cot x+sin x. Writing c=cos x and s=sin x reduces this to (c-s)(cs-c-s)=0, so cs=c+s. Let u=c+s, which is negative on the stated interval. Then u^2=1+2cs=1+2u, giving u=1-√2. Therefore sin(2x)=2cs=2-2√2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2013_AMC_12B_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p105","cnm_h061","cnm_h062","cnm_067"],"id":"parabolic-chord-slopes","label":"Compare slopes of chords of the parabola","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parabolic-chord-slopes":["cnm_h167","cnm_h168","math:reciprocal-trig-identities","cnm_221","cnm_220"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h167","cnm_h168","math:reciprocal-trig-identities","cnm_221","cnm_220","cnm_p105","cnm_h061","cnm_h062","cnm_067"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":9,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, HE = HG is not necessarily correct","reason":"Midpoint relations give AEHF a parallelogram, BH = CD, G the midpoint of BH, and FG = 3AB/4. For A = (0,0), B = (4,0), C = (0,4), the construction gives HE = 2 but HG = √5, disproving B in general.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1955_AMC_12_Q48","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_067","cnm_110","cnm_180"],"id":"solution:midpoint-geometry:bcecd501ec15","label":"Use midpoint geometry","methodDirectNodeIds":{"midpoint-geometry":["cnm_113","cnm_055","cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_185","cnm_174","cnm_071"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_113","cnm_055","cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_185","cnm_174","cnm_071","cnm_067","cnm_110","cnm_180"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":9,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 4/5","reason":"Extend AB and CD to meet at X beyond A and D. In triangle BDX, the exterior angle BDC gives angle BXD = 46° - 23° = 23°, so XD = BD = 1. Since triangles XAD and XBC are similar, XD/XC = AD/BC = 5/9. Hence CD = XC - XD = 9/5 - 1 = 4/5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_12B_Q16","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_066","cnm_067"],"id":"solution:extend-trapezoid-legs:a24dceab75cc","label":"Extend the legs to form similar triangles","methodDirectNodeIds":{"extend-trapezoid-legs":["cnm_069","cnm_117","cnm_138","cnm_268","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_069","cnm_117","cnm_138","cnm_268","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_066","cnm_067"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_058","cnm_066","cnm_067"],"id":"construct-angle-bisector","label":"Create an angle bisector inside the trapezoid","methodDirectNodeIds":{"construct-angle-bisector":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_069","cnm_268","math:angle-bisector-side-ratio"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_069","cnm_268","math:angle-bisector-side-ratio","cnm_055","cnm_p210","cnm_058","cnm_066","cnm_067"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":10,"alignmentIds":["alignment:921578b27047c0dab62684d0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 6","reason":"The equal areas give AE·ED=BE·EC, since the included angles have equal sines. Thus AE/EC=BE/ED, and vertical angles give triangle AEB similar to triangle CED by SAS. Consequently AE/EC=AB/CD=3/4, so AE=14·3/7=6.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_067"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_12A_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_065","cnm_066","cnm_067","cnm_268","cnm_055"],"id":"solution:equal-areas-to-parallel-bases:cecd3b171cbe","label":"Add a common triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-areas-to-parallel-bases":["cnm_p1